# E2: exactness, arm 2, the reference the slide must equal byte for byte. The same matrix plan, lengths, answer budget and audits as
# E1 on c2-packed-tp4-gate-noslide (QWEN_FAST_TP_KV_SLIDE=0: the eager publication chain, the fast path's own non-optimised TP4
# path). Offline, per user: `python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py <E1 results> <E2 results>` (results = the downloaded
# artifact's tree). E1's texts must equal E2's, and so must the SOLO accepted-prefix sequences. The texts alone cannot judge
# the slide: the greedy verifier emits the target's own argmax whatever the drafter holds, so a slide that wrote wrong bytes
# inside the banks gives the same text and only a different (lower) acceptance; a text difference would mean corruption
# OUTSIDE the banks, a prefix-sequence difference is a wrong slide.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card speed window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/speed and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image K0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_GATE_JIT=record as E1.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; per arm an engine build 5-15 min plus 3-10 min of streams (the eager ramp is slow): 25 / 40 /
# 110 min.
# Read: as E1, then compare the texts offline against E1's.
# STOP on a difference from E1 (the compare's exit code 1; 2 means it could not compare: no path records). The chain cannot
# run the compare, so the window's last step is the operator's run of it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-speed-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-noslide
C2_GATE_PLAN=matrix
C2_GATE_LENGTHS=512,1536,4096,16384
C2_GATE_MAX_TOKENS=256
C2_GATE_JIT=record
